sdl3-mixer-gme
==============

This crate is a modified version of Game_Music_Emu: a translation into
Rust of the copy of Game_Music_Emu 0.6.5 ("Game Music Emulators",
Copyright (C) 2003-2009 Shay Green and its other authors, maintained by
Vitaly Novichkov and Michael Pyne; https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu)
that SDL_mixer 3.3.0 vendors (external/libgme/ at SDL_mixer revision
df66ae893c91b0f6fa5d026a195bb278213d007d, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer,
the v0.6.5-SDL branch of https://github.com/libsdl-org/game-music-emu at
7079627509eeb30153f29167baf63d81ab1dfbe7), with the emu2413 1.5.9 YM2413
emulator it carries in gme/ext/ (Copyright (C) 2001-2020 Mitsutaka
Okazaki).

It is NOT the original Game_Music_Emu, nor SDL_mixer's copy of it.

How and when it was changed: on 2026-10-17, the parts of that copy that
SDL_mixer's build of it (its CMake project, as SDL_mixer's CMakeLists.txt
configures it: static, every emulator, no zlib) reaches from SDL_mixer's
GME decoder were translated, function by function, into the Rust source
files in src/, which keep the original copyright notices and comments;
each file says so in a line under its copyright notice. Those are, from
gme/: blargg_common.h, blargg_source.h, blargg_endian.h, Blip_Buffer.h,
Blip_Buffer.cpp, Multi_Buffer.h, Multi_Buffer.cpp (its stereo buffer),
Effects_Buffer.h, Effects_Buffer.cpp, Data_Reader.h, Data_Reader.cpp (its
memory, subset and remaining readers), Gme_File.h, Gme_File.cpp,
Music_Emu.h, Music_Emu.cpp, Classic_Emu.h, Classic_Emu.cpp, gme.h,
gme.cpp, Ay_Apu.h, Ay_Apu.cpp, Ay_Cpu.h, Ay_Cpu.cpp, Ay_Emu.h,
Ay_Emu.cpp, Gb_Apu.h, Gb_Apu.cpp, Gb_Oscs.h, Gb_Oscs.cpp, Gb_Cpu.h,
Gb_Cpu.cpp, gb_cpu_io.h, Gbs_Emu.h, Gbs_Emu.cpp, Hes_Apu.h, Hes_Apu.cpp,
Hes_Apu_Adpcm.h, Hes_Apu_Adpcm.cpp, Hes_Cpu.h, Hes_Cpu.cpp, hes_cpu_io.h,
Hes_Emu.h, Hes_Emu.cpp, Kss_Cpu.h, Kss_Cpu.cpp, Kss_Emu.h, Kss_Emu.cpp,
Kss_Scc_Apu.h, Kss_Scc_Apu.cpp, Sms_Apu.h, Sms_Apu.cpp, Sms_Oscs.h,
Nes_Cpu.h, Nes_Cpu.cpp, nes_cpu_io.h, Nes_Apu.h, Nes_Apu.cpp, Nes_Oscs.h,
Nes_Oscs.cpp, Nes_Vrc6_Apu.h, Nes_Vrc6_Apu.cpp, Nes_Fme7_Apu.h,
Nes_Fme7_Apu.cpp, Nes_Namco_Apu.h, Nes_Namco_Apu.cpp, Nes_Fds_Apu.h,
Nes_Fds_Apu.cpp, Nes_Mmc5_Apu.h, Nes_Vrc7_Apu.h, Nes_Vrc7_Apu.cpp,
Nsf_Emu.h, Nsf_Emu.cpp, Nsfe_Emu.h, Nsfe_Emu.cpp, Sap_Apu.h, Sap_Apu.cpp,
Sap_Cpu.h, Sap_Cpu.cpp, sap_cpu_io.h, Sap_Emu.h, Sap_Emu.cpp, and
ext/emu2413.h and ext/emu2413.c (what the VRC7 uses). Not translated, as
SDL_mixer can't reach them: the file readers and gme_open_file(), M3U
playlists (M3u_Playlist), the custom reader, gme_load_tracks(), the user
data functions, the state saving functions of the sound chips,
Mono_Buffer and Silent_Buffer, and emu2413's rate converter and patch
dump functions. The translation works on Rust types (slices, vectors,
traits and indices rather than pointers, inheritance and unions), and
does something defined where corrupt input makes the C++ code read out of
bounds, read memory it never initialized, crash or hang (the places
marked "FIXME (upstream)" in the source). Otherwise it emulates
bit-for-bit what the C++ code does, which its tests check. The changes
are freely available as part of https://github.com/danielpclark/SDL.

