Game_Music_Emu is licensed under the terms of the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1, or (at your option) any later version, as its
source files say: see COPYING (verbatim from SDL_mixer's copy, its
license.txt). emu2413 is licensed under the MIT license: see
COPYING.emu2413 (verbatim, its ext/LICENSE). So is this crate: its SPDX
license expression is "LGPL-2.1-or-later AND MIT" (MIT for
src/emu2413.rs, LGPL for the rest).

Unlike the rest of the repository, which is under the zlib license, this
crate is under the LGPL. It is a separate crate so that it can be left out
of programs using the rest under the zlib license. sdl3-mixer uses it to
play game music through its `gme` Cargo feature, which is on by default;
build sdl3-mixer with `default-features = false` to leave it (and game
music) out.

The test data in testdata/ (tiny rips, with sound programs assembled for
them) is generated by tools/gen_gme_testdata.py in the repository.
